        {
          "label": "study_title",
          "text": "Thymic CD11c+ cells [scRNA-seq]"
        },
        {
          "label": "study_abstract",
          "text": "This study investigates the dynamics of thymic dendritic cells (DCs) under tumor-bearing conditions and the role of CCR9 in regulating thymic DC homeostasis. CD11c? thymic cells were enriched from wild-type (WT) and CCR9 knockout (CCR9 KO) mice subjected to different experimental treatments. Four experimental groups were analyzed: CCR9 WT mice treated with PBS for 2 weeks CCR9 WT mice bearing MC38 tumors for 2 weeks CCR9 WT mice bearing MC38 tumors for 3 weeks CCR9 KO mice bearing MC38 tumors for 3 weeks Overall design: This dataset contains single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) data of thymic CD11c+ cells isolated from CCR9 wild-type (WT) and CCR9 knockout (KO) mice under different experimental conditions. Four samples are included: CCR9 WT mice treated with PBS for 2 weeks, CCR9 WT mice bearing MC38 tumors for 2 weeks, CCR9 WT mice bearing MC38 tumors for 3 weeks, and CCR9 KO mice bearing MC38 tumors for 3 weeks. After subcutaneous MC38 tumor implantation, CD11c+ cells were sorted from the thymus using BD FACS Aria III and subjected to droplet-based single-cell RNA sequencing using the Chromium Next GEM Single-Cell 5' Reagent Kit v2 (10x Genomics). Libraries were sequenced on a DNBSEQ platform (MGI). Sequencing data were processed using Cell Ranger v7.1.0 (10x Genomics) with the mouse reference (refdata-gex-mm10-2020-A)."
        }
      ],
